{"approved_definition": "Understanding, appreciation, tolerance, and protection for the welfare of all people and for nature. Derives from survival needs that become apparent when people recognize that failure to accept those who are different and treat them justly will lead to strife, and when people become aware of the scarcity of natural resources.", "core_value": "universalism", "sources": [{"entry_id": "8f83c818:entry:3", "journal_entry": "Same day, later. Ordered from Grab because I was too tired to cook. While eating I scrolled past an article about plastic waste in the Java Sea. Closed it, kept eating from the styrofoam container.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "8f83c818:entry:0", "journal_entry": "Had a team standup today and Ravi brought up that our payment processing pipeline is rejecting a disproportionate number of transactions from certain Southeast Asian corridors. The data was right there in the dashboard. Mostly remittance flows, the kind migrant workers use to send money home. Something about the fraud model flagging certain patterns that are just... normal behavior for people sending small amounts frequently.

I knew what I was looking at. I've sat across the table from guys at the worker center who tell me how hard it is to send money back to their families, the fees they pay, the delays. And here's our system making it worse. But when Ravi raised it, the lead just said we'd revisit the thresholds next quarter and moved on. I could have pushed. I had the context, the stories, the data to make a case. But I just nodded and typed something in the chat about checking the logs.

Part of me says it wasn't the right moment, that I need to build a proper case first. But honestly I think I was just worried about being the guy who derails standup with a soapbox moment. My parents always told me not to stick out, keep your head down and do good work. Maybe that advice served them well in a factory town in Fujian. I'm not sure it serves me well here, sitting on information that could change something.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "8f83c818:entry:7", "journal_entry": "Worker center morning. Helped two new guys file their claims. One of them brought me a packet of murukku his wife made. Sat on the bench outside eating it and feeling grateful for this strange second life I have on Saturdays.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Making the world a fairer, better place"}
